<title>UK: American Airlines gets Europe flights back.</title>
<headline>American Airlines gets Europe flights back.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Airlines said flights from Europe to the United States would be back to normal by Sunday after President Bill Clinton intervened to end a pilots strike after 24-minutes.</p>
<p>All 12 flights from London were operating normally without cancellations on Saturday and passengers booked on 14 flights out of Europe had been transferred to other airlines, an American Airlines spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The strike had no impact on London flights and in Europe we had already cancelled and accommodated passengers on other airline flights. Everything will be back to normal by Sunday,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>She said a few passengers had cancelled reservations ahead of the strike but the numbers were &quot;not significant&quot;.</p>
</text>
